  reason: "Observe one actual v1.std.core::build_newline_index return at the retained provider-acquisition boundary while testing gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program. The observer hashes the running seed image and the exact input snapshot before the ordinary compile and hashes the actual returned fields afterwards. It stores only a checked digest in an explicitly selected directory. Explicitly requested observation requires a trace for each source and refuses errors, damaged records and disagreements before entry evaluation. The host owns observation of the running image, immutable file publication and trace delivery. The fresh-process integration control invokes the normal CLI to observe the shadow. This experiment has no route to supply an answer to the compiler. The same standing admits the S1/S4 cache-key fixture: one seed key declaration, v1_compiler.closure_identity::symbol_census_key, plus a test that calls the real compiler in fresh processes. The record layout, integrity hash and create-only publish now have a single seed authority in v1_compiler.closure_identity (shadow_record/shadow_read_prior/shadow_compare_and_record); the production observer and the fixture both call that authority rather than each re-deciding the format, so the stored-record format cannot drift between them. The fixture keys a resolution-dependent build_symbol_index_census answer two ways — bytes-only versus the corrected key over a sorted source pool and sorted closure roster — and proves the bytes-only key serves an intact-but-stale answer while the corrected key recomputes and agrees on a warm repeat. The observer QUESTION and the CLI hook are unchanged; symbol_census_key is keying only and never serves an answer.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "consumers-on-canonical-dependencies" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Retire this question-specific observer when the compiler's common demand trace can report the same pre-production lookup and independent fresh answer for the newline-index question, with missing, unreadable, damaged and valid-but-different prior records distinguishable through the ordinary invocation.",
  current_boundary: "Opt-in at v1_compiler.cli_run.provider_acquire::compile_to_provider_fixed_point_with. The shadow key uses exact running binary bytes, logical file path and source contents. No shared-store publication, producer-skip or performance improvement is implied. The observed output includes every Unicode scalar as well as newline offsets and the file name. For the census fixture the new seed declaration symbol_census_key is keying only; its length-framed preimage is the schema tag, the question tag, the compiler-image identity digest consumed from the existing single authority transform_content_digest (not a re-derived executable read), the sorted source pool as (source file path, module path, source bytes) triples and the sorted closure roster, and it carries only repository-relative source paths, module paths and bytes — no absolute host path, mtime or locator. Binding the source file path jointly with the module path and bytes is required because the SymbolIndex carries file identity (index.file and source-located nodes), so a source-file rename changes the answer; the fixture rename control guards this. The shared record format lives in v1_compiler.closure_identity: a 64-byte record is the stored answer followed by SHA-256 over (schema tag, key, answer), read back under the same schema and refused as corrupt on mismatch; both the newline-index observer and the census fixture pass their own schema tag to the same shadow_record/shadow_read_prior/shadow_compare_and_record authority. The observer's QUESTION and CLI hook are unchanged.",
}
